me saying that  CLG shotcalling is like babysitting he  even claimed the game itself and how was  played saying that League of Legends is  devolving into a game that I don't even  recognize anymore but more than anything  or anyone link flame doublelift  and his fleeting trust in his teammates  link wrote once doublelift loses respect  for anyone  you're [ __ ] dunzo the vitriolic 17  page long document skyrocketed to the  top of the League of Legends subreddit  and exploded across social media the  community dubbed it the dunzo manifesto  immediately cementing its place in a  league Amim history cyrus teased his own  version of the dunzo manifesto when he  retired but eventually decided against  it alas we will never see the dyrus  papyrus so [ __ ] funny  and CLG memed on it too when their  former ADC sub yuna wrote his own dunzo  manifesto which the team submitted to  the league's subreddit from their own  account but if you peel back the memes  and the drama the letter stands as a  unique if very biased look as the NA LCS  at a time when it was still growing into  what it would become today there were  probably a lot of factors that  Leadville in frustration he ran away  from home he put an education at  Berkeley on hold and he was locked into  a contract with CLG that he really  didn't want to be in towards the end but  the lack of infrastructure couldn't have  helped things either CLG had chosen a  coach who was working remotely from  South Korea and the huge support staff  that modern franchised LCS teams have  today were a pipe dream back then links  letter was supposed to be this big mic  drop moment he wanted to expose the  problem with his former team and  teammates and he wanted to shine a light  on a side of League of Legends that the  community had never seen before however  his bias throughout the letter was  called out immediately now the problem  with this farewell letter it was riddled  with inconsistencies he'd say something  and then a paragraph 